import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'blind':('The fear spell that promised confusion',
  'A level fifty necromancer stands surrounded by four young red dragons and considers its blind-creature maneuver, which casts Frighten. The original scored the cast with the confusion attack type: the borg danger model suppresses a confused dragon massively (the probe records a confusion delta of four hundred eight against a fear delta of zero), so the maneuver was valued at nine hundred fifty-five - a phantom the spell cannot deliver, and high enough to win the chooser. The correction scores the cast as the fear effect it is: the maneuver values minus five, exactly what the dedicated Frighten maneuver values.'),
 'control':('Control: the dedicated Frighten maneuver',
  'The dedicated Frighten maneuver, already scored as fear, values minus five before and after the correction with byte-identical logs: the fix changes only the mislabeled maneuver.'),}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/blind-261 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag in ('RATING ','OUTCOME '):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[tag.split()[0].lower()]=match[1].strip() if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The fear spell that promised confusion</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native maneuver valuations</p><h1>The fear spell that promised confusion</h1><p>The Borg has a dedicated Frighten maneuver, scored as the fear effect it is. A second maneuver - named for blinding a creature - also casts Frighten but was scored with the confusion attack type. Against monsters whose danger the model suppresses under confusion but not under fear, the mislabeled maneuver carried a phantom value the spell cannot deliver, high enough to win the chooser and be cast.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">Maneuver value</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the control establishes</h2><p>The dedicated Frighten maneuver, already scored as fear, is valued identically before and after with byte-identical logs: the fix changes only the mislabeled maneuver, whose corrected value equals the dedicated one exactly.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Necromancer level fifty, depth thirty, seed one thousand, lit constructed arena, every class book carried, four awake young red dragons adjacent, avoidance tuned low. The probe records the danger model deltas directly: confusion suppresses each dragon by four hundred eight while fear suppresses nothing here. The measurement calls the public maneuver chooser with borg_simulate set. This isolates the attack-type token, not full autonomous play. No death or survival claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/261">issue261</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);let r=d.rating||'';let m=r.match(/blind=(-?\\d+)/)||r.match(/frighten=(-?\\d+)/);p.querySelector('.num').textContent='Maneuver value: '+(m?m[1]:'n/a');p.querySelector('.state').textContent=d.outcome||'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='blind'?'The original values the Frighten cast at 955 - the confusion suppression it cannot deliver; the correction values it at -5, exactly the dedicated maneuver.':'The dedicated maneuver never changed: -5 either way, byte for byte.';}select.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
